<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Durban Deep Q1 pre-capex net profit dips.</title>
<headline>Durban Deep Q1 pre-capex net profit dips.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending  6.22 vs 8.89</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 17.63 vs 18.46</p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    - underground				710 vs 737</p>
<p>    - sand operations			  291 vs 294</p>
<p>    - opencast operations		    339 vs 342</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    - underground			  213,000 vs 202,000</p>
<p>    - sand operations		    435,000 vs 507,000</p>
<p>    - opencast operations		310,000 vs 290,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    - underground			     3.33 vs 3.65</p>
<p>    - sand operations			 0.67 vs 0.58</p>
<p>    - opencast operations		   1.09 vs 1.18</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - underground			   58,897 vs 54,076</p>
<p>    - sand operations		     45,490 vs 47,405</p>
<p>    - opencast operations		 50,983 vs 48,918</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)			   50,682 vs 56,023</p>
<p>Full name: Durban Roodepoort Deep Ltd, managed by Randgold and Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Rainfall for the quarter amounted to 569 mm which is close to the annual average for the area. Surface and underground production was adversely affected as a result.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
